# Overrides the backend URL the frontend talks to. Leave unset for normal
# local dev -- it defaults to http://localhost:8000/api/, same as before
# this file existed. Set it when the backend is reachable somewhere else
# instead, e.g. through an ngrok tunnel:
#   1. ngrok http 8000            (tunnels the Django dev server)
#   2. copy the https://....ngrok-free.app URL it prints
#   3. VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://....ngrok-free.app/api/
# Must end with a trailing slash, same as the default value.
#
# To actually view the app itself through a tunnel too, separately run
# `ngrok http 5173` for the frontend, and make sure the backend's own
# .env (see backend/.env.example) lists both this tunnel's URL in
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS and its ngrok-free.app host in ALLOWED_HOSTS --
# otherwise Django rejects the tunneled requests outright.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
